  "description_short": "Beloved Sedgefield spot serving fresh fish and chips with harbour views and a relaxed local vibe.",
  "description_long": "Mr Kaai has become a Sedgefield institution, drawing locals and visitors alike to its spot on Uil Street for consistently good seafood and a welcoming atmosphere. The menu centres on what they do best: fresh fish and chips, calamari, and other seafood favourites served without fuss or pretension. It's the kind of place where you know what you're getting, and you're never disappointed.\n\nThe setting is casual and family-friendly, with outdoor seating that makes the most of Sedgefield's mild climate. Portions are generous, prices are fair, and the staff are genuinely friendly. Whether you're stopping in after a beach walk or looking for a reliable midweek meal, Mr Kaai delivers honest food in a town that values authenticity.\n\nIt's not trying to be fancy, and that's exactly why it works. This is neighbourhood dining done right, with a menu that keeps things simple and a reputation built on doing the basics well.",
